---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import CircleCalculator from '@/components/tools/calc2/CircleCalculator.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="circle-calculator">
  <CircleCalculator client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How the circle calculator works</h2>
    <p>
      A circle has one size number: give the radius, the diameter, the circumference or the area, and the
      circle calculator finds the other three.
    </p>
    <pre><code>d = 2r
C = 2πr = πd
A = πr²
r = C ÷ 2π = √(A ÷ π)</code></pre>

    <h2>Worked example</h2>
    <p>
      A circle with a radius of 5 cm has a diameter of 10 cm, a circumference of 2 × π × 5 = 31.4159 cm
      and an area of π × 5² = 78.5398 cm². The animation unrolls the circumference into a straight line:
      it is π times the diameter, a little more than three diameters.
    </p>

    <h2>From the area back to the radius</h2>
    <p>
      A round table top of 1.5 m² has a radius of √(1.5 ÷ π) = 0.691 m, so a diameter of 1.382 m.
    </p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <p>
      The results use π to double precision (15 to 16 significant digits). A measured radius has its own
      error, and the area doubles that error in per cent, because the radius is squared.
    </p>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
